## language boundaries — strictly enforced

- **TypeScript** — all Next.js app logic, API routes, components, database queries
- **Python** — music correlation microservice ONLY (separate repo: yuhnify-music-service)
- **No Java** — do not suggest Java for any part of this codebase
- **No mixing** — do not write correlation logic in TypeScript, do not write API routes in Python

When the music microservice needs to be called from Next.js, use this pattern:
```typescript
const res = await fetch(process.env.MUSIC_SERVICE_URL + "/correlate", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ runs, scrobbles }),
})
```

