## rules — non-negotiable

1. Never write `any` in TypeScript. Ever.
2. Every API route checks auth before any logic. No exceptions.
3. Every database query filters by `userId` — users never see each other's data.
4. Every async operation has try/catch with this error shape:
   ```typescript
   return NextResponse.json(
     { error: string, code: string, retryAfter?: number },
     { status: number }
   )
   ```
5. Every new `src/lib/` function gets a unit test in `tests/unit/`.
6. Validate every API route body with Zod.
7. Use the Prisma singleton pattern — never instantiate `new PrismaClient()` outside `src/lib/prisma.ts`.
8. Run `npm run build` after completing each phase checklist. Fix all errors before moving on.
9. Mobile first — design every component for 390px before desktop.

